 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  J|p=3/2+ for {+35}Cl ground state (2026Su18).                          
 34S  c  1969Pu03: {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He) with a 23.35-MeV , enriched {+35}Cl lead    
 34S 2c  cloride target on thin C backing. Used scattering chamber with |DE-E   
 34S 3c  counter covering the angular domain from 12|' to 30|' in steps of 2|'  
 34S 4c  and 3|'. DWBA calculations (code JULIE).                               
 34S  c  1968Wi20: {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He) with a 34.5-MeV deuteron beam from the Oak 
 34S 2c  Ridge isochronous cyclotron. The target was NaC1 evaporated onto carbon
 34S 3c  backing. The reaction products were detected using a solid-state |DE-E 
 34S 4c  telescope. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced 9 levels, J, |p,         
 34S 5c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from the zero-range DWBA analysis of
 34S 6c  the angular distributions.                                             
 34S  c  1962Cu07: {+35}Cl(d,{+3}He) E=15 MeV. Targets were C4H5Cl2 with        
 34S 2c  evaporated Au. The reaction products were analyzed by a magnetic       
 34S 3c  spectrometer and detected in its focal plane by a CsI crystal. Measured
 34S 4c  |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced two levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic
 34S 5c  factors from the zero-range SALLY-DWBA analysis of the angular         
 34S 6c  distributions.                                                         
